# Deploy configs — not needed inside the image
deploy/
scripts/

# PHASE 106A — narrow re-include for the journal importer.
#
# `scripts/` above stays a blanket exclusion: no other image gets any of it.
# This exception admits ONLY scripts/journal into the build CONTEXT, which is
# what the `journal-importer` stage COPYies. Nothing else changes — the runner
# and migrator stages have no COPY of `scripts/`, so re-including these files
# cannot put them in the web or migration images.
#
# Docker (unlike git) descends into an excluded directory when any `!` exception
# exists, and the LAST matching pattern wins. So ordering matters twice over:
# this exception must come AFTER `scripts/` to take effect, and BEFORE the
# `**/__tests__/` and `**/*.test.ts` rules below so those still strip the
# importer's own test files back out. Both are proven mechanically by
# scripts/__tests__/phase106a-journal-import-path.test.ts and by the image
# audit in the Phase 106A runbook.
!scripts/journal

# PHASE 109-C-UI.2-R8 — a second narrow re-include, for the metering worker.
#
# Same reasoning and the SAME ordering constraints as the block above: after
# `scripts/` so it takes effect, and before the `**/__tests__/` and
# `**/*.test.ts` rules so the worker's own tests are still stripped out.
#
# Unlike the importer, this one IS copied into the runner image, because the
# metering worker service runs the web image with a different command. The file
# it admits is a single dependency-free .mjs that only calls fetch — it holds no
# credentials and opens no database connection, so putting it in the web image
# adds no reachable surface to the running server.
!scripts/industrial

# ATS-S1 — a third narrow re-include, for the ATS AI-review worker.
#
# Narrower than the two above: ONE FILE, not a directory, so nothing else that
# ever lands in scripts/ats/ reaches the build context by accident. Same
# ordering constraints — after `scripts/`, and before the `**/__tests__/` and
# `**/*.test.ts` rules. Only the dedicated `ats-review-worker` Dockerfile stage
# COPYies it; the runner and migrator stages copy no scripts at all.
!scripts/ats/ai-review-worker.mjs

# Test files
**/__tests__/
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx
**/*.spec.ts
**/*.spec.tsx
vitest.config.*

